# Two balls that together cover a ball with a 2-limb center (milestone2.md, "One enclosure
# interface", "Hull, intersection and split of balls"): ball_split_1 on the sum of two limbs, the
# point c plus the balls of center -h and +h (the 2-limb numbers (-h, 0) and (h, 0), by make_2, so
# that no limb is added to a literal zero) and radius q = max(h, r - h), h = RN(r/2), by
# ball_add_2_full. The first contains [c - r, c], the second [c, c + r]; the whole line and the
# empty set are returned twice, as they are. -h is its own product of the negated radius, as in
# ball_split_1 (no fused result negated).
kernel:        ball_split_2
input:         c = c0 c1
input:         stored r
output:        ca = ca0 ca1
output:        ra
output:        cb = cb0 cb1
output:        rb
requires:      ball c r
ensures:       ball_splits ca ra cb rb from=c,r
min_precision: 3
source:        the point c plus the balls (-h, q) and (h, q), q = max(h, r - h), by the proved ball sum of two limbs (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeBallPredicates2.v ball_split_2_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   through ball_add_2_full, which states what comes out; the special states are selected after an explicit test of the radius

h             = prod(r, const up(1/2))
nr            = neg(r)
hn            = prod(nr, const up(1/2))
g             = sub(r, h)
mg            = lt(h, g)
q             = select(mg, g, h)
fr            = lt(r, const inf)
hs            = select(fr, h, 0)
nh            = select(fr, hn, 0)
ws            = select(fr, q, 0)
cs0           = select(fr, c0, 0)
cs1           = select(fr, c1, 0)
(n0, n1)      = make_2(nh)
(p0, p1)      = make_2(hs)
(a0, a1, ar)  = ball_add_2_full(cs0, cs1, 0, n0, n1, ws)
(b0, b1, br)  = ball_add_2_full(cs0, cs1, 0, p0, p1, ws)
ca0           = select(fr, a0, c0)
ca1           = select(fr, a1, c1)
ra            = select(fr, ar, r)
cb0           = select(fr, b0, c0)
cb1           = select(fr, b1, c1)
rb            = select(fr, br, r)
